A||N||9||Haze_Performance||Brake Upgrade Question||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||08-15-2000||07:08 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo.asp?number=56004&variation=&aitem=1&mitem=13" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo.asp?number=56004&variation=&aitem=1&mitem=13</A> <P><BR>Are rotors the same size as the stock ones?? If not is there any way to get larger 4 Wheel vented & Crossdrilled brake kit?? stock stuff looks like CD's behind the new wheels.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>P.S. The lug size could be 5x100 or 5x114.3<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-15-2000||11:22 PM||||Those rotors are the same size I believe.  If not, they are like 1/4 inch bigger. <BR>I know <A HREF="http://www.raynemotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.raynemotorsports.com</A>  has bigger brake kits.  12 and 13 inch kits, but both are around 3k I believe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> But I also think they sell some sort of kit that is a conversion to bigger brakes from an s-10 I think, that's like 900 dollars.  ||||reg||3
Z||000002||baldlobo||08-15-2000||11:37 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  has brake kits.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-16-2000||01:49 AM||||Same diameter, but thicker because they're vented.  I just bought the Fiero Store kit.  It's from an '88 Grand Am.  Other than the mounting bracket and machined hub, you can get the other stuff from your local auto parts store.  Seems to be decent quality stuff.  I figured it cost about $50 extra to go with the FS kit (assuming you can get the hub machined for about $50) but well worth it to me since it means that I didn't have to grind/fab anything.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-16-2000||03:12 AM||||Go to:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ultimategarage.com/bbfiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ultimategarage.com/bbfiero.html</A> <P>Are these big enough for you?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>If you think the brakes are big check out the price!<BR>(Pics are from the above website)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero1_4.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero3_2.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000005||olympic||08-16-2000||03:29 AM||||They've got 15" rotors for vipers and C5"s ...thats just insane!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||08-16-2000||04:08 AM||||Man.. i would give my left nut for a brake set like that... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>IMHO, nothing makes a car look faster and exotic than a big honkin' shiny brake rotor!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||08-16-2000||10:06 AM||||Sidebar:  Proof that the rear brakes don't do nearly as much of the work as the front brakes--The new Corvette Z06 (Americas "real" world class sportscar) has 12.6x1.3" vented disc brakes, but...if you look at the picture (new issue of C & D) you can see that the rear rotor is much smaller than the front.  Braking distance from 70mph: 152 ft.  Not bad for a car that weights almost 3200#.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||08-16-2000||03:24 PM||||Monkeyman, You're right. Most (newer) cars have bigger brakes in the back though to reduce nose dive during braking. Not an issue on a track ready Corvette with a stiff suspension.<P>But, Fiero's have more weight in the back so bigger rear brakes would have a greater effect than on a Corvette.<P>I'd like to use the 12" (11.6"?) Rear F-body brakes on a Fiero (not the crappy mid 80's ones) but the rotors have to be redrilled for the bolt pattern or you have to find a different set of hubs with the 4.5" spacing.||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||10-27-2000||01:57 PM||||Pontiaddict,<P>I pulled this up on search... <P>How does one find out what size spindles other cars have?  I am interested in a y-body swap, but have not been able to locate any information on the y-body spindle size.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
